---
description: Create a Next.js App Router page and its section components with nextjs-page-dev (no test authoring)
---

Run the `nextjs-page-dev` skill end to end for this target, and route every new section component through `nextjs-component-dev`:

$ARGUMENTS

Creation only:

1. Resolve the route, locales, and component directory from `docs/project.json` and `lib/routes.ts`.
2. Scaffold `page-spec.md` with §7 page edge cases (metadata, JSON-LD, boundaries, locale routing) and present the implementation plan for approval.
3. Implement `page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `generateMetadata`, JSON-LD, and `generateStaticParams()`; populate dictionaries for every locale.
4. For each new section or child component, activate `nextjs-component-dev` and follow it end to end (surface folder, skeleton, dictionary keys).
5. Run `verify-page` and `verify-dev` for each new component; fix implementation defects. Existing targeted tests may be run read-only for feedback.
6. Do **not** write, edit, or scaffold tests, test plans, E2E specs, or runner configuration. Test authoring is owned exclusively by the `nextjs-test` skill and runs as a separate step after creation.
7. Work in an isolated `agent/<slug>` worktree; present the review and merge into `main` only after the user approves.
